# Line-ending policy for the knowledge base.  Added 2026-08-25 by maria (R1).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  On 2026-08-25 the audit found instance-general/index.md
# and formal-methods/index.md rewritten with CRLF by a Windows editor.  The real
# change was 6 lines; the diff was 1,099.  core.autocrlf is `false` on this
# machine, so git would have committed the CRLF verbatim and every subsequent
# `git log -p` on those files would have been unreadable.
#
# The whole point of putting the KB under version control (R1) is that the
# history answers "what actually changed and who changed it".  A line-ending
# flip destroys that answer silently, and it is invisible in the editor that
# causes it.  So the normalization is enforced here, in the repo, rather than
# left to each agent's git config.
#
# Effect: text files are stored LF in the object database regardless of what
# the working tree holds.  Nobody has to remember anything.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
# Binaries: never touch.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary

# ARTIFACTS ARE BYTE-EXACT.  Added 2026-10-14 by maria (R1).
# The rules above exist to stop an editor's CRLF flip from turning a 6-line change into a
# 1,099-line diff in hand-written text.  They were never meant for artifacts, and they were
# silently rewriting them: kkm2023-conflict-resolved/artifacts/kkm2023.csv is the authors' file
# with CRLF line endings (33,391 lines), its paper.json records the sha256 of THOSE bytes, and
# `*.csv text eol=lf` made git store LF -- so every fresh checkout held data that was no longer
# the authors' and failed its own recorded checksum.  A checksum on a file the repository is
# allowed to rewrite is the false defect this knowledge base exists to avoid.
# Code under reanalysis/ stays normalized; only artifacts/ is exempt.
papers/*/artifacts/** -text
